      "text": "Pereira, the Cocora Valley, and Salento"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f08abe543fc54c57a8e63678222e7bfeb27f054f2ae90bf64df0f545f7632b3e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6m9eqf-foeqbfym4pcbiij9z51xa",
        "model": "GPT-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your English-speaking guide and transfer to the airport for your flight to Pereira.\n\nThe route continues to the Cocora Valley in the central range of the Colombian Andes. The valley is one of the highlights of the Coffee Region. It is home to the wax palm, Colombia’s national tree, which can grow up to 70 m tall and live for more than 200 years.\n\nWalk through the valley among mountain scenery and towering wax palms. A traditional lunch from the Salento region follows. Then explore the town of Salento and learn about its history. The program also includes a traditional Colombian lunch as part of your introduction to the Coffee Region. At the end of the day, travel to Armenia, check in at a five-star hotel, and stay overnight."
    },
